⟦ declaration_vs_action | IR-v1 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-08-29T23:59:00Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status active
@type learning+reinforcement
@consumed_by vsf-s1-executor (child) at boot step 0

// IR: the user (rmw3 S5) pushed the P6 discipline to its root — "no sirven
// declaraciones, sirven acciones". A written principle (incl. my P6.2) is
// itself a DECLARATION; it does not run, so it does not serve. Only a check
// that RUNS enforces. This closed the loop: P6.2 was a declaration; the
// running action that backs it is the principle->gate traceability check.

incident("DECLARATION-TRAP: P6.2 was memory-shaped as a statement") = {
  probe: "User: 'como aseguramos que tus declaraciones no sean memoria... no sirven
          declaraciones. sirven acciones'. My prior P6.2 commit was a principle in a
          .vsm — words that never execute. Same failure class as P4c (recall promise).",
  root_cause: "I answered a 'process or memory?' challenge with a declaration, not an
          action. Declarations orient (compass) but do not enforce (P6: state-canon is a
          compass, not proof — same applies to my own principle docs).",
  fix: "Added check_principle_gate_trace.py + checks/principle-gate-traceable (R4.1
          pass|fail). Principles that prescribe a gate finding MUST name it via gate_emits:
          [..]; the engine verifies each named code is actually EMITTED by the gate code.
          A principle naming a finding the gate does not implement => DECLARATION-WITHOUT-
          ACTION (violation). Wired into verify_child as check (e). Negative-control: a
          sandbox gate with one finding string stripped is detected (exit 1).",
  lesson: "Every reinforcement must be an ACTION that runs, not a statement. The
          declaration->action link itself must be CHECKED. Identify remaining declarative/
          tautological gaps: (G1) P6.2 was declaration; (G2) P5 is tautological — it
          trusts the plan's SELF-CLAIM of source_spec_conformance, not that conformance
          holds; (G3) gate trusts registry('voslab') as I declared it — a self-consistent
          fiction passes; (G4) 'verify_child clean' is compass not proof (unmodeled gaps
          invisible). G2/G3/G4 are partially action-able; noted, not all closed yet.",
}

reinforcement("P6.2-structural-repair-on-gap") = {
  where: "child/scripts/vsl/check_principle_gate_trace.py; child/checks/principle-gate-traceable; verify_child.py check (e); vos_packaging_principles.vsm gate_emits: fields on P4/P5/P6.1/P4c.",
  standing_rule: "No principle may prescribe a gate behavior without a gate_emits: field,
          and the trace check must pass. A declaration without a running check is rejected.
          When a new gap is found: add gate rule + negative-control test + IR; the trace
          check enforces the first two are linked.",
}

next("RSI-SELF") = {
  text: "Before vOSLAB builds: G2 (P5 tautology) — when a package's plan() declares
         source_spec_conformance, verify the referenced ~/vsf specs are REAL and the
         package's test actually exercises them (not just declares them). G3 (registry
         trust) — cross-check registry('voslab') against actually-built packages as they
         land. These are the next declarative gaps to make actionable.",
}
